   "how": {
    "tpl": "Running watts of everything on: {{out.running_w|int}} W. Each motor's jump at start is its starting watts minus its running watts; only the largest jump is added, because one motor starts at a time: {{out.running_w|int}} W + the largest jump = {{out.peak_w|int}} W. The larger of that peak and {{out.running_w|int}} W × {{out.margin|2}} is {{out.sized_w|int}} W; ÷ {{out.pf|2}} ÷ 1,000 = {{out.recommended_kva|2}} kVA, so {{out.standard_kva|1}} kVA.",
    "text": "Running watts of everything on: 2,040 W. Each motor's jump at start is its starting watts minus its running watts; only the largest jump is added, because one motor starts at a time: 2,040 W + the largest jump = 3,840 W. The larger of that peak and 2,040 W × 1.25 is 3,840 W; ÷ 0.8 ÷ 1,000 = 4.8 kVA, so 5 kVA."
   },
   "submit": "Find the starting watts",
